**Nightwatch at the Museum** is a first-person psychological horror game set in Indonesia, post-1990s Asian financial crisis. Work is rare, and you need it.

You play as **Raja**, a newly hired night guard at the Museum — a former Dutch colonial residence turned heritage site, named after a long-gone Javanese noble family whose history still lingers within its walls.

---

The patrol is mandatory. So is the report. So is showing up the next night, and the night after that. Quitting isn't on the table. That's the job. That's all it is.

Then what you see no longer matches what you write down. There are scorch marks nobody can explain, and the further you patrol, the less the official story holds together. You're not the first guard to start asking questions. The others aren't here anymore.

And something… or someone, in this museum needs you to stay.

---

## Features

- **Slow-burn horror** rooted in Java & Dutch Colonial vibes
- **Cross into a distorted version of the building** when you get too close — and find your way back
- **Your choices close the night** — your job, your conscience, your life. All three decide how it ends
- **Investigate** through logbooks, old newspapers, and labels that don't match the records
